    "text": "Let the foot of perpendicular of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> on the plane passing through the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then the distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> from the origin is",
